t number of times.\n`WeatherClient.get` now retries when the server returns 503, making at most 3 attempts in total. I ran it against a local test server and it behaved as intended:\n\n| Server behavior | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| Healthy | returns the data | 1 |\n| 503 twice, then 200 | returns the data | 3 |\n| 503 on every request | raises the 503 error | 3 |\n| One 500 | raises right away | 1 |\n\nHow it works (all in `weather.py`):\n- Python's HTTP library raises an error for a 503. `get` catches that error and waits `backoff * 2**attempt` seconds before trying again. With the new `backoff` setting at its default of 0.5, the waits are 0.5s and then 1.0s.\n- Any HTTP status other than 503, or a 503 on the last attempt, is raised to the caller as before.\n- Network errors and timeouts are not retried; you only asked for 503.\n- The attempt limit is a class constant, `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3`.\n\nI didn't add a test file to the repo.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 35180, "requests_cache_write": 141720, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7483240000000001, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1632, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial14", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 87, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:49:19.876335+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 20.353, "t_checker_s": 2.395, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1644, "tokens_cac